      "solution": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    // Read the number of customers\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n\n    // Array to store the frequency of each time (0 to 100)\n    int counts[101] = {0}; \n    int t;\n\n    // Read inputs and tally them up in a single pass\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &t);\n        counts[t]++;\n    }\n\n    long long total_wait_time = 0;\n    long long current_running_time = 0;\n\n    // Iterate through our frequency array\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 100; i++) {\n        // If we have customers with this wait time, process them\n        while (counts[i] > 0) {\n            current_running_time += i;\n            total_wait_time += current_running_time;\n            counts[i]--;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Print the result (using %lld because we used long long)\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", total_wait_time);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "statement": "A coffee shop has [[M]] baristas. Each barista prepares one drink at a time.\n\n[[N]] customers arrive throughout the day. Customer [[i]] arrives at minute [[A]]i and orders a drink that takes [[T]]i minutes to prepare.\n\nA drink may start only when:\n\nthe customer has already arrived, and\nthe assigned barista is not busy.\nWhen several customers are waiting, the serving order may be chosen freely. Drinks cannot be interrupted once preparation has started.\n\nThe wait time of customer [[i]] is defined as:\n\n<div style=\"border: 1px solid #555; padding: 10px; margin: 10px 0; font-style: italic; text-align: center;\">\nwait<sub>i</sub> = (minute the drink is ready) − [[A]]<sub>i</sub>\n</div>\nFind the minimum possible total combined wait time:\n\nwait1 + wait2 + … + wait[[N]]\nAll baristas are free at minute 0.",
